* slotted pour, matched grid pitch 0.3 mm, plane nhinc 3, trace 7x5 r2, f 1e+07 Hz
* FastHenry deck written by pour_decks.py -- OpenSim pour loop (ExtractionTests.AReturnThroughAPour_GoesRoundASlot)
.units mm
.default sigma=58000
* return pour: uniform plane, corner nodes half a cell inside the 12 x 6 mm outline so the
* node cells tile the pour exactly; pitch 0.3 mm, 40 x 20 nodes
Gpour x1=-2.85 y1=-2.85 z1=-0.0175
+ x2=8.85 y2=-2.85 z2=-0.0175
+ x3=8.85 y3=2.85 z3=-0.0175
+ thick=0.035 seg1=39 seg2=19 sigma=58000
+ nhinc=3 rh=2
* slot: remove nodes i=19..20, j=3..16 (cell centres inside x 2.7..3.3, y -2..2); removed cells span x 2.7..3.3, y -2.1..2.1
+ hole rect (2.85,-1.95,-0.0175,3.15,1.95,-0.0175)
+ nps (-0.15,-0.15,-0.0175)
+ npe (5.85,-0.15,-0.0175)
* the trace (one segment: its current is the same along its whole length)
Ns x=0 y=0 z=0.335
Ne x=6 y=0 z=0.335
Etr Ns Ne w=0.4 h=0.035 nwinc=7 nhinc=5 rw=2 rh=2
* far end joined by the real connection below; port from the trace start to the plane under it
* real end connection (OpenSim IdealEndConnections = false): wire of radius 0.2 mm as one
* square filament of the same area, from the trace end down to the plane mid-plane z=-0.0175
Nv x=6 y=0 z=-0.0175
Ewire Ne Nv w=0.354490770181 h=0.354490770181
* plane copper over to the grid node standing in for the spot (single filament)
Nb x=5.85 y=-0.15 z=-0.0175
Ebar Nv Nb w=0.4 h=0.035
.equiv Nb npe
.external Ns nps loop
.freq fmin=10000000 fmax=10000000 ndec=1
.end
